@nvpohanh re the reproducibility note in your review:

> The **Accuracy Tests** and **Speed Tests and Profiling** sections give the model, GPU, TP size, and EAGLE settings, but no commands.

Added a "How to reproduce" section to the description: the exact `sglang.launch_server` command, the aiperf invocation for the InferenceX AgentX replay (scenario `inferencex-agentx-mvp`, public dataset `semianalysis_cc_traces_weka_062126_256k`, the concurrency / duration / trajectory settings used), the GSM8K setup (20 questions, greedy, max 8192 tokens, same server with the launches on vs off) with the equivalent `sglang.test.few_shot_gsm8k` command, and the kernel microbenchmark script pasted inline with its H100 output. The agentic trace is the public SemiAnalysis dataset that ships with aiperf, so the end-to-end table is rerunnable from the description alone.
